 "verdict": "RUNG (known models reproduce argmax_census_instruct at the same seed): 2 compared, worst error 0.00e+00. Identical, so this screen measures F144's quantity. SCREEN of 7 candidates at seed 20260803 (of 11 attempted): granite-3.1-2b-instruct 0.000 (none); Phi-4-mini-instruct 0.000 (none); Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct 0.573 (funnel); SmolLM2-360M-Instruct 0.990 (funnel); Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct 0.000 (none); gemma-2-2b-it 0.719 (fragmented); Falcon3-1B-Instruct 0.000 (none). 4 candidate(s) NEVER LOADED and are UNSCREENED, not rejected -- internlm2_5-1_8b-chat (ValueError); EXAONE-3.5-2.4B-Instruct (AttributeError); bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T-bf16 (ImportError); OLMo-2-1124-7B-Instruct (ResourceExhausted). These are environment failures (cache corruption, transformers-version config incompatibility), not properties of the models, so they remain open candidates and the screen's coverage is lower than the candidate list suggests.  PRIMARY, candidates landing in the pre-registered band (0.2, 0.8) on BOTH seeds: Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct (0.573, 0.573), gemma-2-2b-it (0.719, 0.708). 2 of 7 landed in band on the screen seed, 2 survived confirmation. This is the cohort M3b needs -- models with room to move by more than tolerance in BOTH directions. SECONDARY, Falcon3-3B-Instruct's raw arm on 4 census seeds: 0.6146, 0.7708, 0.7917, 0.6771 (mean 0.7136, sd 0.0827). The spread is real, not a two-seed accident, so its tolerance genuinely swamps its domain shifts and F149's refusal to read its +0.146 template rise was correct. BOUNDARY: a CONVENIENCE cohort -- 5 cached models plus a pre-specified extension -- screened on ONE statistic with 96 starts. The yield is NOT a population estimate and no rate may be quoted from it; the only output that counts is the LIST of models that qualify.",
